xenoblade chronicles 3 is the latest  game in monolith soft and tetsuyu  takashi's anthology xeno series what  that means is that similar to the final  fantasy series while the overall  gameplay and ideas are similar amongst  entries the story and characters are  completely fresh  so with that said what do we know about  xenoplay chronicles so far well here's  everything you need to know  xenoblade chronicles 3 is set in the  world of ionios which is notable for its  two major warring nations of kevis and  agnes every being from kevis and agnes  is raised to be a soldier and only has a  10 year life span which they refer to as  their 10 terms there's a mark on at  least one of the factions next that  indicates which term they're on the  ultimate honor for those born in nations  is to live out their full 10 terms and  then partake in a homecoming ceremony  given by their queen during which she  sends the soldier's spirits to the great  beyond  what the purpose of this is or what  happens to these characters after they  receive a homecoming ceremony is  something currently shrouded in mystery  since they're born fighting is all  members of these nations learn and know  as these nations exist in a state of  perpetual war while this is the base  your story focuses on six soldiers three  from kevis and three from agnes while on  a special mission these two enemies run  into each other and naturally end up  fighting until a mysterious figure leads  them on a quest to find sword march from  the 24 minute nintendo direct it sounds  like part of their goal will be to bring  peace to the two warring nations by  defeating the real enemy and restoring  world order to my understanding this  real enemy is called the consuls it  seems to me either these consoles or  other enemies if it's not the console  exist to eat the kevis and agnes for  their life energy during the nintendo  direct there was a line about certain  enemies not needing food or water to  survive but rather life itself  hence why i think this it could be that  the consoles or another enemy could be  pulling the strings to have the caves  and agnes kill each other for their life  energy but that's purely my speculation  and the reason for both the war and why  the consuls are presiding over it is a  mystery of the story we're also told  that the killing between the two nations  has to do with filling one's own flame  clock however what this flame clock is  or what makes it so important is  currently unknown the enemy specifically  says during a nintendo direct trailer to  our characters that if unchecked  oroboros will lead this world to ruin  therefore they must be erased notably as  i'll talk about in a bit our characters  can use the power of oroboros to bond  together and transform in battle so  perhaps this is another of the main  enemy's motivations so while the kevis  and agnes are constant war it seems like  there's a bigger enemy at play here and  similar to previous xenoblade chronicle  games probably some mysteries  surrounding your existence that will be  uncovered  we do see that through fighting together  for a common goal our main characters  come to befriend each other and come to  share a will to live in the now instead  of constantly fighting xenoblade  chronicles 3 is set in the massive world  of ionios ionios is filled with various  terrain and a multitude of enemies while  there is plenty to explore for the main  quest there are also many hidden areas  included for you to discover through  exploration every major location you  visit is saved as a landmark with quick  traveling available to it as soon as you  find it there are also quest routes you  can activate which will put a line on  the map showing you exactly what route  to follow for your current quest  some of the monsters in the world only  appear at specific times so xenoblade  chronicles 3 will also include the  ability to quickly change the time  however it's not clear if this is only  available in certain areas like response  or colonies or you can do this at any  point  colonies are the base camps for both  nations the colonies act as the game's  towns with stories dining options which  will give your party various temporary  stat boosts depending on what you eat  and various characters some of whom can  impart quests the game also seems to  have a character quest tree which  visually shows how these characters are  related to each other and by what quest  within the colonies are furonos which  are mobile bases and weapons of war  outside of colonies there are also rest  spots your characters can utilize here  you can cook using collected materials  cooking will give you various temporary  boosts just like dining within a colony  you can also craft gems here according  to the trailers it states to strengthen  your abilities by looking deeper into it  it looks like this is a crafting system  where you can craft various weapons  shields or other such useful in-battle  items and these crafted items will have  better effects than if you bought the  weapon you'll be able to discuss  information you heard from the various  residents you met at the colonies or  perhaps other places and choose to take  on their side quests here  the combat in xenoblade chronicles 3  takes place on the field and happens  once you encounter an enemy and draw  your weapon or they engage you you'll  control one character at a time while  duking it out with these enemies but for  the first time ever in a xenoblade  chronicles game you can switch which  character you control at any time each  of these party members has a role to  fill to ensure your victory with every  class essentially boiling down to  attacker defender and healer your  abilities are called arts and each of  these arts is assigned to a button on  the switch corresponding to the  on-screen visual making it easier to  execute and also know if an art is  available or not to use these arts have  a variety of effects that you'll have to  cleverly utilize during their best  moments during combat situations you can  also string together arts and perform a  combo of breaking down the enemy's guard  toppling them over launching them in the  air and smashing them back down there  may be other types of combos available  but we definitely know about this one  thanks to the latest overview trailer  similar to combos there are also chain  attacks you can sign your characters  each of the six main characters has a  specific class type although  interestingly you can actually change  each character's class as you please and  none of them are stuck to their original  class combining classes seems like it  will be an important mechanic in the  game as this will determine which arts  and general stats each character has  while also allowing you to find and  assign combos to your characters to form  your ideal party  some of the classes we know are sword  fighter zephyr medic gunner tactician  heavy guard ogre guardian commander  incursor and war medic the exp you get  from battles helps raise the class rank  of the current class you've selected for  each character allowing you to learn and  assign master arts these arts are unique  in that unlike the other arts that are  class specific you can assign master  arts to any class you choose for your  character meaning it will be key to  switch characters classes as you play  through the game in order to get them  various master arts you can gain allies  in the form of a seventh party member  while only one of these allies can help  at a time it seems like you'll  permanently gain these allies and be  able to swap them in and out to suit the  situation these allies called heroes  also have their own unique classes  separate from the main characters  once you befriend them you can even  reassign your main party members to have  these classes as well each of the main  characters has another character they'll  be able to interlink with this fuses the  two characters you choose together into  a mech-like form called an oroboros for  a limited set amount of time  these auroboros also have special arts  however not constrained by the same  limits as the characters on their own  each aura boros has two forms and the  form you see depends on which character  you have controlling the oroboros  both the appearance and moveset of the  auroboros alters depending on who you  have taking the lead for completing  battles you'll gain soul points which  you can use on a skill tree for your  oroboros to learn new arts and make them  stronger xenoblade chronicles 3 releases  july 29th 2022 with additional content  releasing later this year and into next  year through a xenoblade chronicles 3  expansion pass for an additional cost  and that's everything you need to know  about the upcoming xenoblade chronicles  3. are you a fan of this series or if  not excited to try a brand new rpg for  the switch let us know
 

